## Debugging

```bash
# Verbose Ansible (run from repo root)
ansible-playbook ansible/playbooks/site.yml -i ansible/inventories/prod -vvv

# Test single task
ansible dns-01 -i ansible/inventories/prod -m shell -a "systemctl status AdGuardHome"

# Check facts
ansible dns-01 -i ansible/inventories/prod -m setup

# Validate syntax
ansible-playbook ansible/playbooks/site.yml -i ansible/inventories/prod --syntax-check
```

## Important Design Decisions

### Uniform User Management

All hosts (Proxmox, LXC containers, VMs) use the `eric` user with:
- SSH key authentication only (no passwords)
- Passwordless sudo (`NOPASSWD: ALL`)
- Root SSH disabled (`PermitRootLogin no`)

LXC containers are unprivileged (UIDs mapped) and services run as non-root users (adguard, unbound). Postfix runs as root (standard for mail servers).

### ZFS Safety

Ansible configures ZFS properties but NEVER creates/destroys pools. Pool management is manual-only (too critical to automate).

### Split DNS

- Internal (*.esweiss.com) via AdGuard rewrites
- External (*.ericsweiss.com) via Terraform/Cloudflare
- HA with dns-01/dns-02, adguardhome-sync replication

### CI/CD (GitLab)

- **Canonical source**: https://git.ericsweiss.com/eric/weisssrv (GitLab)
- **GitHub mirror**: https://github.com/ericsweiss/weisssrv (read-only, auto-synced)
- **Pipeline**: `.gitlab-ci.yml` with stages: lint, ai-review, validate, test, security, gate, deploy, maintenance
- **Infrastructure runner** (`gitlab-runner-privileged`): Tag `infrastructure`, privileged, handles ALL weisssrv CI/CD jobs
- **Shared runner** (`gitlab-runner`): Tag `k8s-deploy`, unprivileged, `runUntagged: true`, for other GitLab projects
- **Default tag**: `default: tags: [infrastructure]` routes all weisssrv jobs to infrastructure runner
- **Secrets**: 1Password service account (`OP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN` CI variable)

